# Obsessive Pursuit: two sacrifices are X = 2: two counters and no lifelink (the threshold is three), and a permanent the
# OPPONENT sacrifices is not one "you've sacrificed". Bot1 sacrifices two Clues ({2} each) on turn 3 and Bot2 sacrifices its own
# Lotus Petal in that same turn before the attack, so Bot2's sacrifice would make it three if it counted. The Inspector
# attacks as a 3/4 without lifelink: Bot2 loses 3 and Bot1 gains nothing (18 after the two Pursuit triggers).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Obsessive Pursuit
Thraben Inspector
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Lotus Petal
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Obsessive Pursuit.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Thraben Inspector.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Lotus Petal.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Clue Token.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Clue Token.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Lotus Petal.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Attack(Thraben Inspector > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Thraben Inspector.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Thraben Inspector.Toughness = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Thraben Inspector.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Thraben Inspector.Keywords = (absent)
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot2.Graveyard = Lotus Petal
